1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,938
Neanderthals disappeared as

2
00:00:01,938 --> 00:00:03,888
a distinct population, but

3
00:00:03,888 --> 00:00:06,050
some of their ancestry continued.

4
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:08,962
Many people with ancestry outside

5
00:00:08,962 --> 00:00:11,050
Africa carry roughly one to

6
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:13,700
two percent Neanderthal ancestry.

7
00:00:13,700 --> 00:00:16,000
The estimates vary by population

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:16,975
and method.

9
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:19,037
The geography is also more

10
00:00:19,037 --> 00:00:21,350
complicated than a clean split:

11
00:00:21,350 --> 00:00:23,412
later migrations helped bring

12
00:00:23,412 --> 00:00:25,525
Neanderthal-related ancestry

13
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:27,825
into some African populations.

14
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:30,400
The reason is interbreeding.

15
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,175
Some children of encounters

16
00:00:32,175 --> 00:00:33,838
between sapiens and archaic

17
00:00:33,838 --> 00:00:35,500
groups had descendants who

18
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,900
contributed to later populations.

19
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:40,100
That does not make anyone alive

20
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,175
today a different human species.

21
00:00:42,175 --> 00:00:43,938
All living people are Homo

22
00:00:43,938 --> 00:00:45,025
sapiens.

23
00:00:45,450 --> 00:00:46,962
And an ancestry percentage

24
00:00:46,962 --> 00:00:49,000
is not a ranking of intelligence,

25
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,325
worth, or authenticity.

26
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:53,800
The surprising part is simpler:

27
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:55,875
a distinct branch can disappear

28
00:00:55,875 --> 00:00:57,525
while pieces of its ancestry

29
00:00:57,525 --> 00:00:59,175
continue elsewhere.

30
00:00:59,625 --> 00:01:01,375
Replacement and mixture can

31
00:01:01,375 --> 00:01:03,100
both belong to the same human

32
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:04,050
history.
